## Skill Invocation

The `git-repository-management` skill has `disable-model-invocation: true` —
the `skill` tool will NOT list it. This is intentional (prevents token waste
from auto-triggering). When this workflow tells you to "run
git-repository-management", do NOT hand-roll the work. Instead:

1. Locate the skill at `~/.agents/skills/git-repository-management/SKILL.md`
2. Read `SKILL.md` and follow its workflow (it may instruct you to run
   `scripts/refresh.sh` first, then read `INSTRUCTIONS.md`)
3. Execute the skill's scripts, references, and decision tree as directed
4. The `skill` tool's inability to find it is NOT evidence the skill is
   unavailable — explicit workflow instructions override
   `disable-model-invocation`
